/**
 * Optional risk-engine configuration override.
 *
 * The engine works with zero configuration -- every value here has a
 * built-in default (see ../engine/src/Config.php). To change something,
 * copy this file to "engine.php" in this same directory:
 *
 *     cp adguard/config/engine.php.example adguard/config/engine.php
 *
 * then edit only the values you want to change. Anything you omit keeps
 * its built-in default -- you do not need to repeat the whole structure.
 *
 * The filename matters: RiskEngine\Config::load() reads exactly
 * adguard/config/engine.php (or whatever the RISK_ENGINE_CONFIG
 * environment variable points at). A file saved under any other name is
 * silently ignored, so a threshold you "changed" would never take effect.
 *
 * Loaded with `require`, so it must return a PHP array.
 */
